The total circumference is the sum of the circumferences of each circle:

\[
C_{\text{total}} = 2\pi(5 + 10 + 15 + 20)\ \text{cm}
                 = 2\pi(50)\ \text{cm}
                 = 100\pi\ \text{cm}
\]

Numerically:

\[
100\pi \approx 314.16\ \text{cm}
\]

So the combined circumference of the four circles is **\(100\pi\) cm (≈ 314.16 cm)**.
